From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:28:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] chrome_content_browser_client: give Shade's request filter
 its frame

WillCreateURLLoaderFactory passes its frame to ghost::blocking's
MaybeProxyURLLoaderFactory as well: each request the filter blocks then
counts for the tab whose page made it, which the protections panel shows.
Pages, their subframes and dedicated workers have a frame here; shared
and service workers don't, and aren't counted.

Why: the frame is the only link from a URLLoaderFactory to its tab.
Upstream: not upstreamable: product-specific blocking
Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 52fdcb8663156195713f8ab467caba72243a709f..24a23eb4933d9434c177e3277e5303a1e2872173 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -6671,8 +6671,8 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::WillCreateURLLoaderFactory(
     network::mojom::URLLoaderFactoryOverridePtr* factory_override,
     scoped_refptr<base::SequencedTaskRunner> navigation_response_task_runner) {
   // First, so that blocked requests reach no other interceptor.
-  ghost::blocking::MaybeProxyURLLoaderFactory(browser_context, isolation_info,
-                                              factory_builder);
+  ghost::blocking::MaybeProxyURLLoaderFactory(browser_context, frame,
+                                              isolation_info, factory_builder);
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_EXTENSIONS_CORE)
   auto* web_request_api =
